<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 691</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr was a brother of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-allah-ibn-al-zubayr">Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr</a> and his governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-fitna">Second Fitna</a>. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a>, he defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mukhtar-al-thaqafi">al-Mukhtar al-Thaqafi</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a> in 687. He was killed in 691 fighting the Umayyad caliph Abd al-Malik at Maskin, which returned Iraq to Umayyad rule.</p></div>
